new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f4f06e0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/difftests/tests/physical_storage/operations/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Physical address operations
+
+This CPU/Vulkan difftest reuses the compiletests' `operations_body.rs` shader.
+It compares all 768 output bytes for three wrapping-integer seeds under the
+default and qptr pipelines, each with Rust dev and release optimization.
+The shader reads a nested address-containing aggregate, writes and reloads
+through separately loaded aliases, and preserves volatile Function accesses.
+Compiletest snapshots check the unused volatile load, which readback alone
+cannot observe.
+
+The private Vulkan host requires Vulkan 1.3, `shaderInt64`,
+`bufferDeviceAddress`, `vulkanMemoryModel`, and coherent host-visible memory.
+Missing support writes explicit skip metadata. Native errors fail the case.
+The host owns two disjoint 32-byte ranges and supplies a 16-byte push root.
+It checks actual addresses and source/guard bytes before normalizing only
+address fields for CPU comparison. No fabricated address is dispatched.
+Every submission completes before mapping, reuse or retirement. An uncertain
+submission/wait failure aborts before pending objects can be destroyed.
+The native runner is private and accepts only this shader's unsafe contract.
+
+Run from the repository root using `cargo difftest physical_storage`.
+Without nextest, the same harness is available through
+`cargo test --release -p difftests --test difftests -- physical_storage`.
+Both require the tool configuration appropriate to the compiler dependencies.
+The fixture also supports shader-only inspection through
+`cargo run --release --manifest-path tests/difftests/tests/Cargo.toml -p physical-storage-operations-vulkan --features difftest/use-compiled-tools -- --compile-only OUTPUT_DIRECTORY`.
+An optional second argument after a normal harness config path retains the
+exact four executed modules. Use Cargo to supply the codegen library path.
+Native case events mean dispatch completed. The harness's byte comparison
+determines pass/fail. Hardware skips and unexecuted high addresses are not proof.
